  "worked_solution": "We need to find the level of caffeine in the blood between $t=2$ and $t=3$ hours after drinking a cup of coffee. To calculate this, we find the level of caffeine in the blood after $2$ hours, and we subtract from it the level of caffeine in the blood after $3$ hours. So we need to evaluate\n\n$$\nC(2)-C(3).\n$$\n\nThe level of caffeine in the blood after $2$ hours is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C(2) & =140\\cdot {(0.9)}^{2} \\\\  & =140\\cdot 0.81 \\\\  & =113.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe level of caffeine in the blood after $3$ hours is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C(3) & =140\\cdot {(0.9)}^{3} \\\\  & =140\\cdot 0.729 \\\\  & =102.06.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the level of caffeine metabolized between $t=2$ and $t=3$ hours after drinking a cup of coffee is\n\n$$\n113.4-102.06=11.34.\n$$",
